Think: Filter the index for entries modified within the last 24 hours by comparing each entry's timestamp (converted to epoch) against the epoch cutoff for "24 hours ago", and save matches to the candidates file.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F'\t' -v cutoff="$(date -d '24 hours ago' +%s)" '{
 t=$2;
 sub(/\..*/,"",t);
 gsub(/[-:]/," ",t);
 split(t,a," ");
 epoch=mktime(a[1] " " a[2] " " a[3] " " a[4] " " a[5] " " a[6]);
 if(epoch >= cutoff) print $0
}' temp_usr_check/usr_file_index.txt > temp_usr_check/usr_recent_candidates.txt
